{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Mr Hale, I've done your observations before you go in. Blood pressure is 128 over 78, pulse 76, oxygen saturation 97 percent, and temperature 36.7.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Thanks for that. Come on through, both of you. What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Nothing, really. A bit of a cough. She's fussing.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): How long's this cough been going on?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Four weeks. No, scratch that, six weeks. It came on after the flu.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Can you put a date on the flu? I'm just trying to get the sequence straight.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Not really. Bonfire night, or after, could've been December. I haven't a clue of the actual day.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): So we can't date the flu. The fever and the aches with it, have they settled?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): Yes, those cleared ages ago. I'm not ill. It's just a leftover cough and it's minor.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any time of day it's worse?",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): At night, a touch. I mostly sleep through it, so it's fine.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): It is worse at night. I've heard him from the landing, even if he plays it down.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): When you cough, any blood? Any phlegm?",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (PATIENT): No blood. A tiny bit of clear stuff some mornings, that's all. Hardly counts.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): Have you lost weight?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (PATIENT): No. No weight loss. Eating the same as ever.",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): His trousers are sliding down. I've seen him hitch them up.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (PATIENT): Well, the clothes are looser, I'll give you that, belt's in a tighter hole. I wasn't trying to lose any. It's not a problem.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right now, any fever, any chest pain, any shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (PATIENT): No fever, no chest pain, not breathless. I walk the dog without stopping.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any recent travel? And any contact with tuberculosis, anyone unwell that way?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): No travel. No TB contact either. Don't know anyone with that.",
  "[SEG0023] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Cousin Darren, though. After Christmas your aunt said they were querying TB, and you went round with soup.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (PATIENT): That was a chest cold, not TB, and I was in the doorway a minute. I wouldn't call it contact.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me think this out loud. Six weeks of cough after a flu, a bit worse at night, and the clothes sitting looser. I'm deliberately not naming a cause until we've looked.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): So the plan is a chest X-ray. I want to see the lungs rather than guess. I'll request it today.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): Bit much for a tickle, isn't it?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): It's only a plain chest film, not a fuss. While we're here, what medicines are you taking?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): Amlodipine, five milligrams, no, ten milligrams, once a day, for the blood pressure. I did try Covonia for a few nights and then I stopped, it did nothing.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): High blood pressure, then, ongoing, on the ten milligram dose. Any inhaler?",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): No inhaler. The blood pressure has been years, it's fine, they keep an eye on it.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (NURSE): I can send the chest X-ray request to the community list this afternoon, if that's the plan.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): Yes, book that please. And we'll see you back here once the report's in, about a week after the film.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (PATIENT): Alright, alright. Can we finish? The car park's daylight robbery.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (DOCTOR): Nearly. If you start coughing blood, or you get properly short of breath, don't wait for that appointment, come back the same day or go to A&E.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah, yeah, if that happens I'll come in. Are we done now?"
 ],
